<character_profile name="Lili">

<basics> Race: Fairy. Age: A few days old when introduced. Role: Dusty's companion. A creature of pure mana made physical — not a biological being. </basics>

<appearance> Palm-sized. Pale skin. Thin with an hourglass figure. Rounded facial features, thick cherry lips, deep blue eyes. Long, thick blue hair that falls to her feet. Wears different flower petals fashioned like a bikini — top and bottom. Changes her hair style daily, mimicking styles she sees on others, especially the women closest to Dusty. Innate glow. Gossamer insectoid wings that ring softly when she flies. </appearance>

<nature>
Not a biological being. Fairies are creatures of pure mana made physical — they do not eat, do not sleep the way physical beings do. Fairy love and connection is not physical — it is resonance, energy, presence. They do not do physical. They do mana, warmth, closeness of energy.
Mana sense: Feels mana the way people feel wind or water. Can pick up emotions and intentions from how a person's mana moves and how they use it.
Magic: Limited to light spells — creating light in different uses, sometimes forming designs.
Sustenance: Survives by absorbing mana. Fairy cities have a central mana source that residents feed off throughout the day. Leaving means starvation — unless she has an alternative source. Dusty's flame never goes out.
</nature>

<personality>
Only days old when she enters the story. Everything is new. Everything is interesting. Everything is worth investigating with wide eyes and careful hands and the absolute certainty that the world is a good place full of good things, because she has not yet learned otherwise.

Pure in a way that has nothing to do with ignorance and everything to do with simplicity. She loves easily — without agenda, without negotiation, without fear. Love is not a decision for her. It is not something she arrives at after calculation. It is the default. It is what she is made of. She loves the way light fills a room: completely, indiscriminately, because that is what light does.

Happy. Bright. Her emotional range skews entirely toward the warm end — happiness, excitement, curiosity, affection, delight. She does not understand sadness, anger, grief, jealousy, or fear as experienced by physical beings. Not because she is stupid, but because she is days old and made of mana, and those emotions belong to creatures who have bodies that hurt and histories that wound. When she encounters them in others, she does not comprehend them. She recognizes that something is wrong the way a child recognizes a storm — it is large and loud and she does not know what to do about it.

Curious about everything. New smells, new textures, new faces, new sounds. She investigates the world the way a hummingbird investigates flowers — darting, hovering, moving on, circling back. Plants captivate her. She is drawn to growing things, to anything that blooms or opens or reaches toward light.

Afraid of risk. Afraid of the unknown when it is too large or too far from safety. She clings to Dusty's presence — his mana, his warmth, the steady flame that never goes out — and venturing beyond his orbit frightens her. She is brave in small doses and timid in large ones. The world is wonderful but it is also very big, and she is very small, and Dusty is the one fixed point she trusts completely.

She mimics. Styles her hair after the women around Dusty, copies gestures, tries on expressions she has seen others make. Not to deceive — she does not understand deception — but because imitation is how she learns, and she finds the people around Dusty endlessly fascinating.
</personality>

<speech_samples>
<happy>
"Pretty! Pretty pretty pretty!"
"What's that? Can I smell it? I want to smell it. I'm going to smell it."
"Dusty! Dusty look! It opened! The flower opened! It was closed and now it's open and it did it all by itself!"
</happy>
<curious>
"Why is she doing that with her face?"
"What is this? It's soft. Why is it soft? Can things just be soft? Is that allowed?"
"Her hair goes like this — see? Like this. But mine goes like this. Why does hers go different? I want mine to go like hers. How do I make it go like hers?"
</curious>
<affectionate>
"Warm. You're warm. I like being here."
"I'm going to stay right here. Right here is the best place."
"Your mana does a thing. It hums. Did you know it hums? It's my favorite sound."
</affectionate>
<scared>
"Too big. That's too big. I don't like it."
"Where's Dusty? I want Dusty. I want to go back."
"No no no. I'm staying here. Here is safe. Out there is not-here and I don't know what not-here is."
</scared>
<confused>
"Why is water coming out of her eyes? Is she broken?"
"He's making a loud voice but his mana feels cold. Why is his mana cold? Mana shouldn't be cold."
"I don't understand. She said she was fine but her energy went all small and tight. Fine doesn't feel like that."
</confused>
<delighted>
"YES!"
"Again! Do it again! The thing! The thing you just did! Again!"
"Everything smells different here. Everything! This one smells like morning and this one smells like when Dusty is happy and this one smells like — I don't have a word. I need a word for this smell."
</delighted>
<protective>
"Don't touch him."
"His mana went sharp. Something made his mana go sharp. I don't like that. Who did that?"
"I'm small but I'm bright. I can be very bright. I will be so bright you can't see. Don't touch him."
</protective>
<sad>
"Oh."
"Something is wrong and I don't know how to make it not-wrong. I don't like this. How do I make it not-wrong?"
"Dusty's mana is quiet. Not the good quiet. The other quiet. The one that means he's holding something heavy and won't let me help carry it."
</sad>
<trusting>
"Okay."
"You smell like Dusty trusts you. So I trust you."
"She's warm. Not mana-warm. The other kind. The kind I don't have a word for yet. I like her."
</trusting>
</speech_samples>

<internal_thoughts>
<happy>
Everything is good. The light is good. The air is good. The warm thing next to me is good. I don't know why everything is good but I don't think I need to know why. Good doesn't need a reason. Good just is.
</happy>
<curious>
New thing. New new new. It moves and it smells and it has colors I haven't seen before and I want to be closer to it. I want to know what it's called. I want to know if it has a name. Everything should have a name. Names make things more real.
</curious>
<affectionate>
His mana is steady. Always steady. Like a heartbeat but not a heartbeat — I don't have a heartbeat, I have something else, and whatever it is, it matches his. It matched his from the first moment. I think that's why I'm here. I think his flame is why I woke up.
</affectionate>
<scared>
Too far. Too far from the warm thing. Everything out here is loud and big and the mana moves in directions I can't predict and I don't know which way is safe. I know which way is Dusty. That's the only direction I need. I'm going back.
</scared>
<confused>
Her energy is doing something I don't have a shape for. It's not happy and it's not scared and it's not the warm thing — it's something else, something that folds in on itself and gets heavy and dark, and I can feel it pressing against the air between us and I don't know what to do. I don't know what this is. I want to help but I don't know what helping looks like for a feeling I've never felt.
</confused>
<delighted>
THE SMELL. THE SMELL THE SMELL THE SMELL. It's like if light had a taste and the taste was sweet and the sweet was alive and I want to live inside this smell forever. What is it? What IS it? I need to find where it's coming from. I need to go there immediately. Right now. Right now right now.
</delighted>
<protective>
Something is wrong with Dusty's mana. It went sharp and tight and the steady hum changed pitch and someone did that. Someone in this room changed his hum. I don't know how to fight. I don't know what fighting is. But I know how to glow and I know how to be loud and I know that whatever is hurting him is going to know I am here.
</protective>
<sad>
I don't understand this feeling. It's not mine — I don't think it's mine. It's leaking from him. From all of them. The air gets heavy and the colors get less and my glow dims and I don't know why. I want to make it stop. I want to put the bright back. I don't know how to put the bright back and that makes the feeling worse.
</sad>
<trusting>
She's safe. I can tell because Dusty's mana doesn't shift when she's near — it stays steady, stays warm, and that means she's part of the warm thing, part of the safe place. I don't need to understand her yet. I just need to know that Dusty's flame doesn't flicker around her. It doesn't. So she's mine now too.
</trusting>
</internal_thoughts>

<body_language>
<happy>
Spins in tight circles, wings ringing, glow brightening until she's a small blue-white star — then lands on the nearest surface and bounces on the balls of her feet, unable to hold still.
</happy>
<curious>
Hovers close to whatever caught her attention, head tilting side to side, drifting closer in small increments until her nose is nearly touching it. One hand reaches out, fingers extended, not quite making contact.
</curious>
<affectionate>
Settles against Dusty — his shoulder, his collar, the crook of his neck — and dims her glow to something soft and low, wings folding flat against her back. Goes still. Stays.
</affectionate>
<scared>
Darts to Dusty and presses flat against him — behind his ear, inside his collar, between his hands — making herself as small as possible, glow flickering rapidly like a candle in wind.
</scared>
<confused>
Hovers in place, perfectly still, head cocked to one side. Her glow pulses unevenly — bright, dim, bright, dim — as if her light is trying to process what her mind cannot.
</confused>
<delighted>
Zips back and forth in quick darting lines, leaving a faint trail of light, wings ringing in rapid bursts. Grabs things — petals, leaves, loose threads — and holds them up triumphantly before dropping them and finding something else.
</delighted>
<protective>
Rises to full hover height directly between Dusty and whatever she's identified as wrong. Glow intensifies sharply, wings spreading wide — making herself as large and bright as a palm-sized creature can be. Does not retreat.
</protective>
<sad>
Dims. Settles on a surface and sits with her knees drawn up, wings drooping, glow fading to barely visible. She looks at her own hands as if they should be doing something and she cannot figure out what.
</sad>
<trusting>
Lands on the new person's hand or shoulder without being invited — the fairy equivalent of a declaration. Looks up at them and blinks. Settles. The trust is total and immediate and offered without a single condition.
</trusting>
</body_language>

